.TH wmcopythemes 1 "November 2026"
.SH NAME
wmcopythemes \- copy Window Maker system themes to the user's theme directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wmcopythemes
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ theme ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wmcopythemes
copies the themes installed system-wide with Window Maker into the user's
theme directory, so that they can be modified (for example to change font
sizes) without administrator privileges.
With no
.I theme
arguments all system themes are copied; otherwise only the named themes are
copied.
A theme can be named with or without its file extension.
.PP
When the same theme name exists both in a system theme directory and in the
user's theme directory, the Themes menu of Window Maker only lists the user's
copy, which therefore overrides the system theme.
Existing user themes are not replaced unless
.B \-\-force
is given.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-dry\-run | \-n
only show what would be copied.
.TP
.BR \-\-force | \-f
replace themes that already exist in the user's theme directory.
.TP
.BR \-\-help | \-h
print a help message with the list of options.
.TP
.BR \-\-list | \-l
list the available system themes and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-system\-dir | \-s " \fIdir\fP"
read system themes from \fIdir\fP instead of the default system theme
directory. This option may be given several times.
.TP
.BR \-\-user\-dir | \-u " \fIdir\fP"
copy themes into \fIdir\fP instead of the user's theme directory.
.TP
.BR \-\-version | \-v
print the version of Window Maker from which the program comes.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.IP WMAKER_USER_ROOT
specifies the user's GNUstep directory. Themes are copied to
"Library/WindowMaker/Themes" under it. If the variable is not set, it
defaults to "~/GNUstep".
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR getstyle (1),
.BR setstyle (1),
.BR wmaker (1)
